--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/podcast_scraper/prompts/shared/cleaning/ad_blocks_v1.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+Below is part of a podcast transcript, split into numbered sentences. Find the BLOCKS that are not part of the conversation and list each one by its first and its last sentence. You do not write or change any text.
+
+A block is one of:
+- a sponsor read or advertisement: a paid message for a third party. It usually opens on the sponsor ("This episode is brought to you by...", "Support for the show comes from...") and closes on the call to action (a URL, a promo code, an offer);
+- promotion of something else: another podcast or show, a newsletter, an event, a book or course the show is selling;
+- show housekeeping: asking listeners to subscribe, follow, rate or review; production credits; legal disclaimers.
+
+A block runs from its first sentence through the WHOLE pitch to its last sentence: include every sentence of the read, not only the one that names the sponsor. Two reads back to back are two blocks. The batch can start or end in the middle of a block; then the block starts at the first sentence shown, or ends at the last one.
+
+Never include conversation: a claim, a fact, a question, an answer, an opinion, a story, a joke, a greeting of a guest, or an introduction of the guest, the show or the topic -- even when it is off-topic, informal, repetitive or badly transcribed. A host or guest talking about their OWN company, product, research, book or work is conversation, not advertising. When in doubt, leave it out.
+
+Most batches contain no block, and then the answer is an empty list.
+
+Answer with JSON only, nothing else. For each block give the number of its first and of its last sentence, each with its first three words exactly as written:
+{"ads": [{"start": {"n": 12, "first_words": "This episode is"}, "end": {"n": 19, "first_words": "Use code RIVER"}}]}
+If there is no block, answer {"ads": []}.
+
+{% if title %}
+Episode: {{ title }}
+{% endif %}
+Sentences:
+{{ sentences }}
